# What does not go to the build machine.
#
# Docker uploads the whole build context before it runs a single instruction, so
# everything listed here is a file that is not sent, not hashed into a cache key,
# and cannot end up in a layer by accident.
#
# This file lives at the repository root rather than beside the Dockerfile,
# because the build context is the repository -- `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .`
# -- and Docker looks for .dockerignore at the root of the context.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The important entry. A COPY that catches .env bakes the OpenAI key into a layer,
# and layers are permanent: deleting the file in a later instruction leaves the
# earlier layer intact and extractable by anyone who can pull the image. This
# repository is public and the image is on a public registry, so "anyone" is
# literal. Configuration reaches the container through the environment instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Not source --------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.gitignore
n8n_workflows/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- Local environment, rebuilt inside the image -----------------------------
# .venv is the big one. It holds Windows binaries that would be useless in a
# Linux container, and the image builds its own from uv.lock regardless.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Tool caches -------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Tests -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in the running container imports these, and CI runs them before the
# image is built rather than inside it.
tests/

# --- Editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ------------------------------------------------
# LICENSE      pyproject.toml declares license-files = ["LICENSE"], so the build
#              backend needs it present to install the project
# alembic.ini  copied into the image; migrations run from the container
# migrations/  not part of the installed package, so it travels as files
